  "title": "Library Drift and Ratchet: Diagnosing and Fixing Self-Evolving LLM Skill Libraries",
  "summary": "Library drift in self-evolving LLM skill libraries leads to unbounded skill accumulation without outcome-driven lifecycle management, causing performance degradation and false positives. Ratchet addresses this by introducing a minimal governance recipe that lifts held-out pass@1 performance from a baseline of 0.258 to a late-window mean of 0.584, demonstrating its effectiveness.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Library drift in self-evolving LLM skill libraries leads to unbounded skill accumulation without outcome-driven lifecycle management, causing performance degradation and false positives.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Ratchet introduces a minimal governance recipe that lifts held-out pass@1 performance from a baseline of 0.258 to a late-window mean of 0.584.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Eight ablations decompose which governance mechanisms are load-bearing and which are subsumed, providing a concrete playbook for diagnosing library drift.",
